# QUALITY GATES

> **Non-negotiable:** every commit, local included, must pass `npm run verify`.

```bash
npm run verify
```

## Gates

| # | Gate | Cap |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | Repository hygiene | no binaries · no secrets · no file >1 MB · ≤400 tracked files · ≤40 npm scripts |
| 2 | Cyclomatic complexity | **≤ 10** per function |
| 3 | Lint | **0** errors, **0** warnings |
| 4 | Tests | all pass |

Enforced by Lefthook on pre-commit and pre-push. Install once: `npx lefthook install`.

## Repository hygiene — the permanent rule

**Git history is forever.** A pushed 200 MB checkpoint is downloaded by every clone, forever. Deleting it later does not remove it.

**NEVER commit:** `.pt .pth .bin .safetensors .gguf .onnx .ckpt .npy .parquet` · `data/` `runs/` `artifacts/` `node_modules/` `.venv/` `.local/` · `.env` `*.pem` `*.key` · anything >1 MB.

**Write heavy output to gitignored directories; promote only the small summary JSON (<100 KB) that proves a gate passed.**

Full doc: `docs/REPO-HYGIENE.md`.

## Never

- `git commit --no-verify` — if the gate blocks you, it is right.
- Raise a cap to make a commit pass. Raising a cap is a reviewable commit that explains why.
- Commit a broken `main`.
